      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Missouri, Iowa and Nebraska Railroad arrived in 1876, sparking Plano’s rapid growth and linking it to regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/plano_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Settlers arrived in the 1850s, drawn to Johns Township’s level prairie lands ideal for farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/plano_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1922, Plano’s 3rd Street business district boasted a drug store, barber shop, lumberyard, and even a billiard hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/plano_iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
